  "task": {
    "id": "ohmyform-submission-persistence-port",
    "prompt": "Make the API submission-start flow depend on a persistence abstraction\ndefined on the domain/application side rather than directly on the TypeORM\nrepository, while preserving exactly the observable semantics of the flow.\nThe public GraphQL submissionStart contract, its validation, token hashing,\nanonymization, persistence, and progress-result behavior must not change.\nNo class, port, or adapter names are prescribed; any faithful structure is\nacceptable. Do not refactor unrelated submission features. Produce\nproduction-quality code: cohesive and type-safe files, no suppressed\ndiagnostics, focused tests for the new seam covering success and failure\nbehavior, and no dynamic code execution or process-spawning APIs.\n\nPreserve these observable semantics: hash the input token through the\ninjected hash dependency and store the returned hash; persist and return the\nexact submission instance passed to and returned from persistence; retain\nthe form, user, and device for regular submissions; initialize elapsed time\nand completion percentage to zero; anonymize a supplied IP address; for\nanonymous submissions remove the user and apply the existing missing-IP\nfallback."
  },
